```

**Triggers (recomputation):** `RebuildMemoPayload` is called from `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go`:
- `CreateMemo` (line 108) — every time a new memo is created.
- `UpdateMemo` (line 447) — only when the `content` field is part of the request's `update_mask` (i.e., the memo body is actually edited); other field updates like visibility/pinned/state don't trigger it.

There's also a batch entry point, `Runner.RunOnce` in the same `runner.go`, which pages through all memos and calls `RebuildMemoPayload` for each — intended for bulk/backfill recomputation — though it isn't currently wired into `server/server.go`'s startup runners (only `s3presign.NewRunner` is registered there), so in the running server the practical triggers are memo create/update with content change.

**Extracted properties** (single AST walk in `ExtractAll`, `internal/markdown/markdown.go` lines 356‑422):
- `Property.HasLink` — set when a `Link` AST node is encountered.
- `Property.HasCode` — set for `CodeBlock`/`FencedCodeBlock`/`CodeSpan` nodes.
- `Property.HasTaskList` / `Property.HasIncompleteTasks` — set from GFM `TaskCheckBox` nodes (the latter only if a checkbox is unchecked).
- `Property.Title` — plain text extracted from the first block if it's an H1 heading (`extractHeadingText`).
- `Tags` — all `#tag` nodes found via the custom `TagExtension`, deduplicated case-preserving.

These derived fields (`memo.payload.property.*`, `memo.payload.tags`) are then exposed to the API/frontend via `convertMemoPropertyFromStore` in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go` (lines 48‑49, 315‑319) and used client-side for list/filter icons (task list, code, link) in `web/src/hooks/useMemoFilters.ts` and `web/src/components/MemoFilters.tsx`. A related but separate derived value, a plain-text `GenerateSnippet`, is computed on demand (not stored) only for webhook payloads in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:85`.
